    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0300" n="194" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg194"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6131/315</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Eastern
                        European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kelley</hi>)<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d206-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-06">April 6, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>If Mr. Litvinoff confirms in writing that Soviet purchases in the United States
                    in 1935 will probably amount to some $30,000,000, I think that we should
                    consider that such assurance is quite adequate and furnishes a satisfactory
                    basis for generalizing to the Soviet Union tariff concessions accorded other
                    countries.</p>
                <p>You will note from the following figures that purchases in the amount of
                    $30,000,000 will involve a considerable increase over Soviet purchases in the
                    United States in recent years:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">American Exports to the Soviet Union</hi>
                </p>
                <table cols="3" rend="width: 50%" rendition="#center" rows="3">
                    <row role="label">
                        <cell>1932</cell>
                        <cell>—</cell>
                        <cell role="num">$12,640,891</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>1933</cell>
                        <cell>—</cell>
                        <cell role="num">8,997,307</cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell>1934</cell>
                        <cell>—</cell>
                        <cell role="num">14,866,515</cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert</hi> F. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Kelley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d206-f1" n="20" type="source" xml:id="d206-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to the Secretary of State, the Under Secretary of State, Assistant
                    Secretary of State Moore, and Assistant Secretary of State Sayre.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
